{
 "_about": "London (level_09): its environment probes' boxes, places, radii and side widths as 0.31a2 authors them, project by project (0.31a2's day_2/3/4, rain_2/3/4 and evening_2/3/4; day_5 and Free for All's day_8 take day_2's). Skhid's London came from an earlier build of the map, where seven probes differ: the boxes of hall_2_floor, hall_box(1) and ladder(1), the places of hall_2_floor and gerkin(3), the side widths of hall_2_floor and gerkin(22), and the radii of gerkin(1), gerkin(3) and hall_box_1_floor(2). Both builds draw the visible probes largest radius first (the same sort in both executables), so the radii decide which probe's reflection lies on top: with radius 5, gerkin(3) ties gerkin_hall_centre; 0.31a2's 4 draws it after. Every London project (merge #2213 first).",
